1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:00,930
That door close button

2
00:00:00,930 --> 00:00:02,302
in the elevator?

3
00:00:02,322 --> 00:00:03,378
Bad news.

4
00:00:03,398 --> 00:00:04,862
Come on, come on, come on!

5
00:00:04,882 --> 00:00:06,162
In many elevators,

6
00:00:06,162 --> 00:00:07,486
it doesn't do anything.

7
00:00:07,506 --> 00:00:08,366
In the US,

8
00:00:08,366 --> 00:00:09,376
accessibility rules say

9
00:00:09,376 --> 00:00:11,066
the doors must stay open

10
00:00:11,066 --> 00:00:12,711
long enough for everyone.

11
00:00:12,731 --> 00:00:13,801
So the close button

12
00:00:13,801 --> 00:00:14,641
often only works

13
00:00:14,641 --> 00:00:16,265
with a firefighter's key.

14
00:00:16,285 --> 00:00:17,615
You're not pressing a button.

15
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:19,040
You're pressing a feeling.

16
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,881
And it's not just elevators.

17
00:00:20,901 --> 00:00:22,951
In New York, a 2004 report

18
00:00:22,951 --> 00:00:24,981
found most crosswalk buttons

19
00:00:24,981 --> 00:00:26,305
did nothing at all.

20
00:00:26,325 --> 00:00:27,453
Any minute now.

21
00:00:27,473 --> 00:00:28,703
Some office thermostats

22
00:00:28,703 --> 00:00:29,853
are fake too,

23
00:00:29,853 --> 00:00:31,353
installed just to stop people

24
00:00:31,353 --> 00:00:32,503
complaining about

25
00:00:32,503 --> 00:00:33,540
the temperature.

26
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,524
They're called placebo buttons.

27
00:00:35,544 --> 00:00:36,534
And honestly?

28
00:00:36,534 --> 00:00:37,384
They kind of work,

29
00:00:37,384 --> 00:00:38,954
because you feel in control.

30
00:00:38,974 --> 00:00:40,164
Now go press one.

31
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:41,442
You know you want to.

32
00:00:41,462 --> 00:00:42,362
Follow for more

33
00:00:42,362 --> 00:00:43,449
hidden designs.
